# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in every working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chart fixtures. Read this before adding a rule above it.
#
# The encoding and the line endings ARE the fixture. This corpus deliberately
# holds Shift-JIS, UTF-16LE and LF-only charts, and at least one whose bytes
# are not valid Shift-JIS anywhere. Normalising any of that silently rewrites
# the thing under test, and the rewrite is invisible in review because the
# rendered diff looks identical.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion. `diff` keeps them reviewable, because a
# change to a chart still has to be readable by a human.
#
# This exemption is load-bearing. scripts/validate.mjs pins every chart's
# SHA-256 so that if this line is ever removed or bypassed, CI fails loudly
# rather than quietly accepting rewritten bytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
charts/** -text diff

# Generated parse snapshots. Held to the same rules as source.
parse/** -text diff
